Carried patch, Windows only: Palace's unit test sources under MinGW.

The upstream test gate builds test/unit, and five of its files do not compile
with MinGW, for the two causes palace/04 fixes in the library itself.
std::filesystem::path does not convert to std::string where its value_type is
wchar_t, so .string() (or .string().c_str()) goes wherever a path meets a
std::string or a const char*: test-postoperatorcsv.cpp (10 sites),
test-lumpedportintegration.cpp (4), test-postoperator-boundary-viz.cpp (3) and
test-schema.cpp (2). And uint is a glibc and macOS typedef MinGW lacks, so
uint(1) and uint(0) become 1u and 0u in test-lumpedportintegration.cpp (4) and
test-romoperator.cpp (10). Nothing a test checks changes, and Linux and macOS
compile the same values.

